This looks like a small Caesar-style salad: chopped romaine with shaved parmesan and a light dressing. It sits on a square plate of roughly 26 cm. The food covers about a third of the plate, in a thin layer, and there are a few leftover pieces.

I estimate about 60 g of romaine, 10 g of parmesan, and 10 g of dressing, which is roughly 80 g in total. The energy is about 10 kcal from the lettuce, 40 kcal from the cheese, and 50 kcal from the dressing, so around 100 kcal. I'll round up to 110 kcal because the dressing amount is uncertain.

